WEBVTT

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.080
I found myself 2011 I started a little

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:05.520
business called Storage Squad. I did

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:07.520
pickup and delivery storage for

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:09.120
students. And naturally, I dove all in

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:11.280
on entrepreneurship. My senior year, I

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:15.040
took a ton of entrepreneurship courses.

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:18.400
One of those courses um was the typical

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:19.920
uh you know uh curriculum of a

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:21.439
entrepreneur course and you go in and

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:23.439
you pitch your idea on day one and then

00:00:21.439 --> 00:00:27.119
you work on your idea the entire

00:00:23.439 --> 00:00:30.480
semester. And um it was 25 kids in the

00:00:27.119 --> 00:00:33.680
class. 24 of them had, you know, tech

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:36.480
startups, new app ideas, uh, things that

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:37.840
they were going to invent. And I had a

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:40.399
service company that picked up and

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:43.040
delivered boxes. And naturally, when I

00:00:40.399 --> 00:00:45.040
pitched that idea, the professor said,

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:46.719
"Okay, what's your moat? How are you

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:48.000
going to scale that business? What makes

00:00:46.719 --> 00:00:50.000
you different than the 20 other

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:52.000
companies who already do this?" And I

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:54.239
didn't have a good answer. My answer

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:55.600
was, I'm just going to answer the phone

00:00:54.239 --> 00:00:57.360
and I'm going to do things a little bit

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:59.520
better than the competition out there

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:01.120
doing it. Well, you fast forward 10

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:03.280
years and I've been able to build a

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:04.879
pretty successful group of companies.

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:08.159
And unfortunately, most of the folks in

00:01:04.879 --> 00:01:10.560
that class who had brand new ideas um

00:01:08.159 --> 00:01:11.760
went and got jobs. So, that's what my

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:14.320
book is all about. That's what I'm all

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:15.760
about is doing common things uncommonly

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:18.000
well and thinking about entrepreneurship

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:20.159
in a new way and thinking about business

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:23.119
opportunity in a new way because the

00:01:20.159 --> 00:01:25.600
media whether it be social media, Shark

00:01:23.119 --> 00:01:28.080
Tank, Product Hunt, all this all these

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:29.439
autobiographies of tech titans which are

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:30.880
unbelievable people. They have everybody

00:01:29.439 --> 00:01:34.079
thinking that entrepreneurship is done

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:36.400
one way. Innovate new idea change the

00:01:34.079 --> 00:01:37.759
world. If you don't have something new,

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:38.720
your idea is important. If you don't

00:01:37.759 --> 00:01:41.040
have something new, you're never going

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:42.640
to make it. And um in my experience in

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:44.240
business, it's the exact opposite. You

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:47.280
can get paid very well to do simple

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:49.439
things and um you can look out there at

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:51.040
companies that exist offering services

00:01:49.439 --> 00:01:53.040
now and you can find a way to compete

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:54.159
just a little bit better. So um that's a

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:55.920
good starting point because that's my

00:01:54.159 --> 00:01:58.640
it's my entire mantra.

00:01:55.920 --> 00:02:01.360
>> Yeah. Doing common things uncommonly

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:02.399
well is is so smart and it you know it

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:04.240
reminds me actually one of the one of

00:02:02.399 --> 00:02:06.399
the lines that I read in the book is you

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:08.879
do not need a revolutionary idea to

00:02:06.399 --> 00:02:10.160
become an entrepreneur. And so I feel

00:02:08.879 --> 00:02:11.440
like yeah, a lot of those people from

00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:13.120
your business class were out there

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:14.319
trying to sell the world on something.

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:17.040
They're trying to sell them on a new

00:02:14.319 --> 00:02:19.280
concept, new idea. Um, but the world is

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:21.120
already sold on a lot of ideas that they

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:22.720
already need. You know, you could take a

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:24.480
small idea that the world already needs

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:26.720
and put a big amount of effort into it

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:28.879
rather than taking a big amount taking a

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:30.160
big idea and trying to launch that idea

00:02:28.879 --> 00:02:32.000
into the world.

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:34.000
>> Yeah. I think the the wealthy people

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:35.920
that I know and when I define wealth,

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:37.280
they do what they want to do when they

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:39.599
want to do it. They have control of

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:40.879
their time. They travel. They play golf.

00:02:39.599 --> 00:02:42.480
They Okay. Yeah. They have financial

00:02:40.879 --> 00:02:43.440
wealth as all but as well, but they

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:46.239
spend time with their kids. They

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:48.239
generally do what they want to do. 99%

00:02:46.239 --> 00:02:50.160
of them started an old-fashioned

00:02:48.239 --> 00:02:53.440
business that already existed. Sure,

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:55.040
they innovated, but it wasn't their idea

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:57.360
that got them wealthy. It was the

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:59.920
execution. It was their ability to sell,

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:02.400
their ability to hire, delegate, manage,

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:04.720
solve problems, make decisions. Those

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:06.800
things are what separated them and

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:09.120
helped them build wealth. And so

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:11.280
everybody thinks they need a

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:12.239
groundbreaking idea. And that's yeah,

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:13.599
that's that's a myth about

00:03:12.239 --> 00:03:16.159
entrepreneurship. It's just not It's

00:03:13.599 --> 00:03:16.159
simply not

